{"id": "EUVD-2026-71248", "enisaUuid": "253cc4d7-d3ae-3317-9646-8f4a50f06f50", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnvmet: fix NULL pointer dereference in nvmet_execute_identify_nslist()\n\nWhen a host issues an Identify command with CNS 07h (Active Namespace ID\nList for a specific I/O Command Set), nvmet_execute_identify_nslist() is\ncalled with match_css set. The command-set filter dereferences req->ns,\nbut this handler never calls nvmet_req_find_ns(), so req->ns is always\nNULL (nvmet_req_init() resets it to NULL). As soon as an enabled\nnamespace with an NSID greater than the requested value exists,\nreq->ns->csi dereferences a NULL pointer and oopses.\n\nBesides the crash, the comparison is logically wrong: to filter the list\nby command set it must test the command set of the namespace being\niterated, not a single fixed value. Use the loop variable ns->csi.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:13:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61dc1a37e04d4003a19095f54883358330034a39", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2bc1e33ff6a558c8ceef7c0077f3ef70a15fcba2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/123d664ac98d6f3464462ad4a530474b91ba9890", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/79aba4c9403419d822972d2851f2a96a2c0531cf"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rf7w-4fpm-954r", "CVE-2026-80813"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ac80a84-83f9-3df9-8c2d-c253ca165d04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61c9967cd63448292a64f9ee9aeb6e2053e3a624 <123d664ac98d6f3464462ad4a530474b91ba9890"}, {"id": "1349b270-0873-3533-a646-dd34b8c9250a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.11"}, {"id": "467277bb-b3a8-35c1-bdfe-77d3c2c5569e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61c9967cd63448292a64f9ee9aeb6e2053e3a624 <79aba4c9403419d822972d2851f2a96a2c0531cf"}, {"id": "4698c334-aaed-3426-aff4-e9876cc7e623", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "6075a5d2-6828-37fc-af1e-42232396869c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6bc15fe5-a99f-34e8-85f2-a2977efa453e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61c9967cd63448292a64f9ee9aeb6e2053e3a624 <61dc1a37e04d4003a19095f54883358330034a39"}, {"id": "7314a0cc-1f96-3296-8c48-d520ca627e52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.47"}, {"id": "8176cdee-5671-3b71-8185-5143e2c9b1cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.1"}, {"id": "a4c62e2c-1e2a-3c37-b6ed-b1d7b6217e3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "61c9967cd63448292a64f9ee9aeb6e2053e3a624 <2bc1e33ff6a558c8ceef7c0077f3ef70a15fcba2"}, {"id": "b18f744c-7578-36e1-86d2-078987d910d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "970d2b24-2ac9-3f6e-a615-7b59e4005970", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}